# Non-membership of j(qᵖ) in the level-M field, p ∤ M

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.jqNModC_prime_not_mem_fullC`
(`20304447-457e-591b-8484-0204b5d74aef`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `cfc162c6-1055-5ff3-81e7-6e439d448f46`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ be a field and write $j =$ `jqModC K` for the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{image in } K
\text{ of } E_4^3\,\eta^{-24}) \in K((q))$, and, for $N \ge 1$, $j(q^N) =$ `jqNModC K N` for its
image under the ring homomorphism `qExpand K N` that multiplies all exponents by $N$. Let $M \ge 1$,
let $p$ be a prime with $p \nmid M$, and let $\zeta$ be a unit of $K$ whose underlying element is a
primitive $(Mp)$-th root of unity. Assume, for every divisor $d \ge 1$ of $M$, both that
$[\,K(j)(j(q^d)) : K(j)\,] = \sum_{e \mid d,\ e \text{ squarefree}} d/e$ (Dedekind's $\psi(d)$, as
`dedekindPsi` is defined) and that the $K$-intermediate field generated by $\{j, j(q^d)\}$ coincides
with the $K$-intermediate field of $K((q))$ generated by all $j(q^{d'})$ with $1 \le d' \mid d$.
Assume further that $j(q^p) \notin K(j)$. The conclusion is that $j(q^p)$ does not lie in the
$K$-intermediate field of $K((q))$ generated by all $j(q^{d'})$ with $1 \le d' \mid M$.

In the formal $q$-expansion model of the function fields of the curves $X_0(N)$, this is the
coprime-level independence step: the degeneracy generator at a prime $p$ stays outside the field
generated by all degeneracy generators of level prime to $p$, provided it already escapes level one.
It is used in the assembly of the level-by-level data for these function fields,
[`ModularCurve.package_of_socket`](thm.html#ModularCurve.package_of_socket).

